 "verdict": "IT TELLS YOU WHICH GENES, NOT WHEN. On 11-point (all targets incl. placebo) NR3C1 occupancy adds +0.0068 held-out R2 over interval identity and gene history -- but a CONSTANT per-gene vector, the gene's time-averaged occupancy with no time resolution at all, recovers +0.0095 of that (139%). Permuting the time axis costs almost nothing (+0.0067) for the same reason, while swapping gene identity destroys it. So GR site occupancy identifies which genes have volatile trajectories; it does not say when they move. That is a static annotation, not dynamics, and Stage 1 remains unsupported. Under per-timepoint quantile normalisation, which makes assay depth irrelevant, the gain is +0.0099. Placebo: CTCF +0.0003, RAD21 -0.0004. Split by half, the occupancy LEVEL contributes +0.0067 and the occupancy CHANGE +0.0013."
